  "body": "Found in the delta review of the merge-time refresh of PR #2822. The code is already on `main` (#2400, #3146). The refresh did not cause it.\n\n`inject_relief_spurs` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs:86-120`) can skip a corner relief that passed the relief filter. This occurs when no pass vertex is within 1e-4 mm of the relief start and no candidate chord clears the center area. The relief is then not cut, and no note tells the user.\n\nThe output is not a gouge: the corner keeps material. But AGENTS.md says \"Log diagnostics. Never hide them.\" The risk can be higher in the rest mode from the previous operations (PR #2822), where the rest center comes from a grid of stock columns.\n\nExpected: each kept relief that gets no spur adds a note that names the corner. Add a test that forces this case.\n",
